---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    name: 'Terms of Service',
  },
];

const lastUpdated = '2026-09-25';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="Terms of service for LocalNodeOps benchmarks, guides, calculators, and the Local Node Docker Stack digital product."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <article class="max-w-reading mx-auto px-lg py-2xl">
    <h1 class="text-display-hero text-primary">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="text-body-md text-secondary mt-xs">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <section class="mt-lg">
      <h2 class="text-headline-lg text-primary">Nature of the content</h2>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-secondary mt-sm">
        LocalNodeOps publishes hardware benchmarks, guides, and interactive
        calculators (such as the VRAM estimator) for informational purposes.
        Benchmark figures and calculator outputs are estimates based on
        published specifications and reference architectures — not
        guarantees of real-world performance for your specific hardware,
        model, or configuration. Verify critical decisions against your own
        testing before making a purchase.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-lg" id="data-license">
      <h2 class="text-headline-lg text-primary">Benchmark and VRAM data license</h2>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-secondary mt-sm">
        The hardware benchmark figures and VRAM calculator estimates
        published on this site — the numeric measurements themselves, not
        the surrounding article text, site code, or LocalNodeOps
        branding — are licensed under
        <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" class="text-accent-primary hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (CC BY 4.0)
        </a>. You may reuse this data, including commercially, provided you
        credit LocalNodeOps and link back to the source page.
      </p>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-secondary mt-sm">
        This license does not extend to: the site's source code, design,
        or branding (see "Open-source content" below); the paid Local Node
        Docker Stack digital product; or article prose, headings, and
        commentary surrounding the data.
      </p>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-secondary mt-sm">
        Model file sizes synced from Hugging Face remain under the license
        terms of their original source repository — CC BY 4.0 applies only
        to our own computed estimates (KV cache, runtime overhead, and
        totals derived from those files), not to the underlying files or
        their source licensing.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-lg">
      <h2 class="text-headline-lg text-primary">Open-source content</h2>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-secondary mt-sm">
        Where a repository or code sample is marked open-source, it is
        provided under the license stated in that repository. Absent an
        explicit license, no permission is granted to redistribute site
        content commercially.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-lg">
      <h2 class="text-headline-lg text-primary">Affiliate and sponsored links</h2>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-secondary mt-sm">
        This site participates in affiliate/referral programs with select
        cloud GPU providers (currently RunPod and Lambda Labs) and with
        Amazon Associates. If you click a cloud GPU affiliate link and rent
        an instance, or click an Amazon Associates link and make a
        purchase, we may earn a commission at no additional cost to you.
        Cloud GPU links are shown as a clearly labeled, separate suggestion
        when a calculated configuration exceeds the VRAM of the local
        hardware profiles listed on this site; Amazon Associates links are
        shown as a labeled suggestion for compatible local consumer
        hardware when a configuration fits within local hardware profiles.
        Neither is ever blended into the benchmark data or the VRAM
        calculator's output itself.
      </p>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-secondary mt-sm">
        The calculator's math (model weight size, KV cache estimate,
        runtime overhead, and which local GPU profiles a configuration
        fits) is computed identically regardless of whether an affiliate
        relationship exists with any provider, and is never adjusted based
        on affiliate revenue. See <a href="/methodology" class="text-accent-primary hover:underline">/methodology</a>
        for the exact formula.
      </p>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-secondary mt-sm">
        As an Amazon Associate, LocalNodeOps earns from qualifying
        purchases.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-lg">
      <h2 class="text-headline-lg text-primary">Local Node Docker Stack (digital product)</h2>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-secondary mt-sm">
        LocalNodeOps offers a paid digital product, the Local Node Docker
        Stack, sold and delivered through Lemon Squeezy, our merchant of
        record. Lemon Squeezy handles payment processing, applicable sales
        tax, and automated post-purchase delivery. By purchasing, you agree
        to the following terms in addition to Lemon Squeezy's own
        purchaser terms:
      </p>
      <ul class="text-body-lg text-secondary pl-lg flex flex-col gap-xs mt-sm">
        <li>
          <strong class="text-primary">License.</strong> Purchase grants a
          single-user license to use the Docker Stack for your own local or
          personal-project deployments. Redistribution, resale, or
          publishing the Stack's contents as your own product is not
          permitted.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-primary">Refunds.</strong> Refunds are
          available within 7 days of purchase. Contact the address on the
          <a href="/contact" class="text-accent-primary hover:underline">Contact page</a>
          to request one.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong class="text-primary">No warranty on the product itself.</strong>
          The Docker Stack is provided "as is." We do not guarantee it will
          be compatible with every hardware configuration, model, or
          existing setup.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-lg">
      <h2 class="text-headline-lg text-primary">No warranty</h2>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-secondary mt-sm">
        Content is provided "as is," without warranty of any kind. We are
        not liable for hardware purchase decisions, configuration choices,
        or outcomes based on information published on this site.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-lg">
      <h2 class="text-headline-lg text-primary">Changes</h2>
      <p class="text-body-lg text-secondary mt-sm">
        These terms may be updated as the site evolves. Material changes
        will update the "Last updated" date above.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>